data.content:
## What Breaks in .NET 11

**Sync I/O on the EF Core Cosmos DB provider is fully removed.** In .NET 10 you could opt-in to sync-over-async; in EF Core 11 that opt-in no longer exists. All synchronous calls **always throw** — no configuration can restore them.

Your affected methods:
- `ToList()` → throws
- `First(...)` → throws
- `Count()` → throws
- `SaveChanges()` → throws

### Fix: Convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This is a **cascading change** — all callers must also become async (`async`/`await` up the call stack). There is no workaround or opt-in to keep sync behavior in EF Core 11 with Cosmos.
